  "summary": "Episode 82 combines a Thumbs Up! China reunion, an emergency-defecation story, a long avoidance-of-love discussion, and two producer auditions. Stephanie's translation/navigation work is correctly elevated from colorful guest detail to essential production labor. The racial acting theory built around eye size, emotion and stardom is rejected as stereotype rather than explanation. The sexual-health section is corrected through consent and safer-sex principles: no is not made permanently nonliteral by marriage or prior play, painful sex should stop, and adequate lubricant reduces friction and injury. ACOG guidance corrects the abortion and miscarriage discussion: ordinary exercise usually does not cause miscarriage, medication abortion and vacuum aspiration are established evidence-based methods, and heavy bleeding can require care. The Crappuccino story remains the title source, while abandoning human waste is identified as a sanitation and worker-safety failure. The hiring material is strongest when it identifies fandom, taste, problem-solving and delegated authority, and weakest when a 23-year-old candidate is pressed for debt, relationship and sexual details. Eight exact public redactions protect private people. Named dialogue remains withheld.",
